# Game Design

## Overview

The game is a simple text-based adventure game where the player can move around a grid-based map, interact with non-player characters (NPCs), collect items, and engage in combat.

## Game Structure

The game will be structured into the following components:

### Game Loop

The game loop will run continuously until the player quits the game. The loop will consist of the following steps:

1. Update game state
2. Render the game world
3. Handle user input
4. Check for collisions and events
5. Update game state again
6. Repeat from step 1

### Game World

The game world will be a 2D grid, where each cell represents a location. The grid will be divided into rooms, each with its own description and features.

### NPCs

NPCs will be represented as objects with their own attributes and behaviors. They will be able to interact with the player, provide information, and offer quests.

### Items

Items will be represented as objects with their own attributes and behaviors. They will be able to be collected by the player and equipped.

### Combat

Combat will be a simple text-based system, where the player can attack or defend against the
